  "functions": [
    "FUNC.VALUE"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "VALUE takes one percent sign anywhere around parentheses, and a euro sign but not a dollar",
  "statement": "VALUE reads parentheses as a negative sign and one percent sign in any of these places: \"(1)%\", \"(1) %\", \"(1%)\", \"(%1)\" and \"%(1)\" are all -0.01. A second percent sign, as in \"(1%)%\", \"%(1)%\" and \"(1)%%\", gives #VALUE!, as does trailing text. The euro sign is read as a currency sign in the recorded en-ZA settings: \"€1\", \"1€\", \"€ 1\", \"€-1\", \"-€1\", \"(€1)\" and \"€(1)\" are 1 or -1. \"$1\" and \"£1\" are #VALUE! there. Currency and percent do not combine: \"€1%\", \"(€1)%\" and \"(R1)%\" are #VALUE!.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "21 recorded VALUE readings.",
